# Frontend UI guardrails

- Reuse existing UI primitives and design tokens when they fit the same role.
- Prefer structural layout fixes over one-off spacing, positional offsets, or selector overrides.
- Avoid duplicate generic components, unnecessary `!important`, and arbitrary z-index escalation.
- Do not over-abstract unstable exploratory UI; temporary one-off values or small duplication are acceptable when they keep experiments easy to change.

Use the `frontend-ui-development` skill for broader workflow and phase-specific guidance.
